# Recipe Platform — Cursor Rules
# Stack: Next.js 16 (App Router) · Drizzle ORM · SQLite · NextAuth.js · Tailwind CSS · TypeScript

---

## General Principles

- Always use TypeScript. Never use `any` — use proper types or `unknown`.
- Prefer Server Components by default. Only use `'use client'` when necessary (event handlers, hooks, browser APIs).
- Follow Next.js App Router conventions strictly (layouts, loading, error, page files).
- Keep components small and focused. If a component exceeds ~150 lines, split it up.
- Never hardcode secrets or API keys. Always use environment variables from `.env.local`.
- Always handle loading and error states explicitly.

---

## Project Structure

Follow this structure exactly:

```
/app
 /layout.tsx
 /page.tsx
 /auth/login/page.tsx
 /auth/signup/page.tsx
 /recipes/page.tsx
 /recipes/[id]/page.tsx
 /recipes/new/page.tsx
 /recipes/[id]/edit/page.tsx
 /profile/[username]/page.tsx
 /profile/me/page.tsx
 /api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts
 /api/upload/route.ts
/components
 /ui/ # Generic reusable UI (Button, Input, Card, Badge, etc.)
 /recipes/ # RecipeCard, RecipeForm, IngredientList, StepList, etc.
 /layout/ # Navbar, Footer, SearchBar
 /auth/ # LoginForm, SignupForm
 /profile/ # EditProfileForm, ChangePasswordForm
/lib
 /db/
   index.ts     # Drizzle client + SQLite connection
   schema.ts    # Drizzle table definitions
   seed.ts      # Database seed script
 /auth.ts       # NextAuth configuration
 /actions/      # Next.js Server Actions
 /validations/  # Zod schemas
 /utils.ts      # Utility functions (cn, etc.)
/types
 database.ts    # Drizzle-inferred types
 next-auth.d.ts # NextAuth type augmentation
/drizzle        # Generated migration files
/data           # SQLite database files (gitignored)
```

---

## TypeScript

- Import database types from `@/types/database.ts`.
- Use Drizzle's `InferSelectModel` and `InferInsertModel` for table row types.
- Define component prop types inline with `interface` for clarity.
- Always type Server Action return values explicitly.

```typescript
// ✅ Good
import type { Recipe } from '@/types/database'

interface RecipeCardProps {
  recipe: Recipe & {
    authorUsername: string
    authorDisplayName: string | null
  }
}

// ❌ Bad
function RecipeCard({ recipe }: { recipe: any }) {}
```

---

## Drizzle ORM

- All table definitions live in `/lib/db/schema.ts`.
- Database connection is in `/lib/db/index.ts` using `better-sqlite3`.
- SQLite database file is at `./data/recipe-share.db` (gitignored).
- Use WAL mode and foreign keys for performance and integrity.
- Always handle query errors with try/catch in Server Actions.
- Use `eq`, `and`, `or`, `like`, `desc` from `drizzle-orm` for queries.

```typescript
// ✅ Good — Drizzle query
import { eq } from 'drizzle-orm'
import { db } from '@/lib/db'
import { recipes } from '@/lib/db/schema'

const [recipe] = await db
  .select()
  .from(recipes)
  .where(eq(recipes.id, id))
  .limit(1)

if (!recipe) notFound()

// ❌ Bad — ignoring errors
const recipe = await db.select().from(recipes).where(eq(recipes.id, id))
```

- Use `.returning()` when you need the inserted/updated row back.
- Use `text('col', { mode: 'json' })` with `.$type<T>()` for JSON columns.
- Generate migrations with `npm run db:generate`, apply with `npm run db:push`.

---

## Authentication (NextAuth.js)

- NextAuth configuration lives in `/lib/auth.ts`.
- Route handler is at `/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts`.
- Use JWT strategy with credentials provider.
- Always use `auth()` from `@/lib/auth` to get the session in Server Components and Server Actions.
- Never trust client-sent `user_id` values — always derive from the session.
- Protect routes via `proxy.ts` (Next.js 16 middleware convention) — never rely solely on UI hiding.

```typescript
// ✅ Good — derive user_id from session
import { auth } from '@/lib/auth'

const session = await auth()
if (!session?.user?.id) return { error: 'Unauthorized' }
// use session.user.id

// ❌ Bad
const userId = formData.get('user_id') // never trust this
```

- Password hashing uses `bcryptjs` with 12 salt rounds.
- Session augmentation types are in `/types/next-auth.d.ts`.

---

## Server Actions

- All mutations (create, update, delete) must be Server Actions in `/lib/actions/`.
- Always validate input with Zod before touching the database.
- Always verify the user session at the top of every Server Action using `auth()`.
- Return a typed result object, never throw raw errors to the client.

```typescript
// ✅ Good pattern for Server Actions
'use server'

import { auth } from '@/lib/auth'
import { db } from '@/lib/db'
import { recipes } from '@/lib/db/schema'
import { recipeSchema } from '@/lib/validations/recipe'

export async function createRecipe(data: unknown) {
  const session = await auth()
  if (!session?.user?.id) return { error: 'Unauthorized' }

  const parsed = recipeSchema.safeParse(data)
  if (!parsed.success) return { error: parsed.error.issues[0]?.message ?? 'Invalid input.' }

  try {
    const [recipe] = await db.insert(recipes).values({ ... }).returning()
    return { data: recipe }
  } catch {
    return { error: 'Failed to save recipe.' }
  }
}
```

---

## Components & React

- Use `async/await` in Server Components for data fetching — no `useEffect` for data fetching.
- Only use `'use client'` for: forms, interactive UI (likes, saves), modals, toast notifications.
- Use React Hook Form + Zod for all forms. Never use uncontrolled raw form elements.
- Use `useTransition` for optimistic UI updates on likes/saves.
- Never fetch data inside Client Components if it can be done in a Server Component and passed as props.

---

## Tailwind CSS

- Use Tailwind utility classes only. No inline styles, no CSS modules, no external CSS unless absolutely necessary.
- Use `clsx` or `cn()` (from `tailwind-merge`) for conditional class names.
- Mobile-first responsive design. Start with base styles, layer up with `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`.
- Use a consistent spacing scale. Stick to `4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64px` (Tailwind's `1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 12, 16`).

---

## Image Uploads

- Always validate file type and size before uploading (max 5MB, jpg/png/webp only).
- Upload via the `/api/upload` route which saves to `public/uploads/recipe-images/{userId}/`.
- Generate unique filenames using `crypto.randomUUID()` to avoid collisions.
- Store the public URL path (e.g. `/uploads/recipe-images/...`) in the database.
- Use Next.js `<Image>` component for all images — never raw `<img>` tags.

---

## Forms & Validation

- Define all Zod schemas in `/lib/validations/`.
- Share the same schema between client-side validation and server-side Server Action validation.
- Use descriptive error messages in Zod schemas that can be shown directly to users.

---

## Error Handling

- Every page must have an `error.tsx` sibling file.
- Every async route segment must have a `loading.tsx` with a skeleton UI.
- Never show raw database error messages to the user — log them server-side and show a friendly message.
- Use toast notifications (e.g. `sonner`) for mutation feedback.

---

## Performance

- Use Next.js `<Image>` with explicit `width` and `height` or `fill` for all images.
- Paginate all list queries — never fetch unbounded lists. Default page size: 12.
- Use `Suspense` boundaries around async Server Components for streaming.

---

## Naming Conventions

| Thing | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Components | PascalCase | `RecipeCard.tsx` |
| Hooks | camelCase with `use` prefix | `useRecipeLike.ts` |
| Server Actions | camelCase verb phrases | `createRecipe`, `deleteComment` |
| Database tables | snake_case plural (in SQLite) | `recipes`, `saved_recipes` |
| Schema variables | camelCase (in TypeScript) | `savedRecipes` |
| Environment variables | SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE | `AUTH_SECRET` |
| Zod schemas | camelCase with `Schema` suffix | `recipeSchema` |
| TypeScript types/interfaces | PascalCase | `Recipe`, `UserProfile` |

---

## Testing

### Unit (Vitest)

- Unit tests live in `/tests/unit/` as `*.test.ts` (Zod validations, `cn()`, pure helpers).
- Run with `npm run test:unit`. Config: `vitest.config.mjs`.

### Playwright (E2E)

- E2E tests live in `/tests/specs/` with Page Object Model classes in `/tests/pages/`.
- Test fixtures for authenticated sessions are in `/tests/fixtures/`.
- Test environment variables are in `tests/.env.test` (copied from `tests/.env.test.example`).
- Tests run across Chromium (desktop + Android) and WebKit (iPhone + iPad).
- Use the `setup` project for authentication state; other projects depend on it.
- Never hardcode test user credentials in specs — read from `process.env`.
- GitHub Actions: smoke tests on PRs to `dev` (`smoke.yml`); full suite after smoke or on PRs to `main` (`full-suite.yml`). See `.github/BRANCH_PROTECTION.md` for public-repo setup.

---

## What NOT to Do

- Do not use the Pages Router (`/pages` directory). App Router only.
- Do not use `getServerSideProps` or `getStaticProps`.
- Do not use `useEffect` for data fetching.
- Do not store sensitive data (passwords, tokens) in localStorage.
- Do not use `any` in TypeScript.
- Do not commit `.env.local` to version control.
- Do not use raw `<img>` tags — always use Next.js `<Image>`.
- Do not write mutations directly in components — always use Server Actions.
- Do not use `router.push` after a Server Action for revalidation — use `revalidatePath` instead.
- Do not store plain-text passwords — always hash with bcryptjs.
